  "response_text": "The stack pool is a reserved section of memory used to store stacks for both the operating system and all user threads. Every thread needs its own stack to keep track of function calls, local variables, and context during execution, and the OS itself also needs a separate stack for handling exceptions, interrupts, or code that runs outside of any thread. In future labs, when we create multiple threads, each thread will be given a stack from the stack pool. This prevents threads from interfering with each other\u2019s memory and ensures the OS has a stable place to run its own logic. Without a dedicated stack pool, running multiple threads safely wouldn\u2019t be possible.\\n",
